# General

Prefer extracting reusable logic into hooks instead of duplicating behavior.

Tables must use GlobalTable

Before creating any new component or template, check for an existing one and reuse it. If unsure whether one exists, ask before creating a new file.

Each file must have a single clear responsibility. If a file grows beyond one responsibility, split it. Do not mix layout, state management, and data fetching in the same file.

# Fields & Inputs

All form fields MUST use FieldShell with a field variant.

Do NOT render raw <input>, <select>, or <textarea> directly in pages.

Validation, error text, helper text, and icons must be handled by FieldShell.

# Modals & Popovers

All modals MUST use ModalTemplate.

File Management

Make sure to check if you need to delete old files whenever you create new files, so there isn't file bloat.

If a new file replaces an old file, delete the unused file and remove unused imports.

Do not leave unused imports, unused exports, or dead files. If functionality is removed or replaced, clean up immediately.

# Icons

- Any svg icons I import, add to the icon library and then import from the icon library into the component.
- Rule: Always import from @/components/icons (your library), never from lucide-react directly in components


# State Management

Do not add multiple useState calls for modals, selection, or form values.

All page-level UI state must live in a single useReducer using activeModal, selection, and drafts.

Only one modal may be open at a time, and closing a modal must reset its draft state.

Child components must remain presentational and may only use local state for purely visual UI (e.g. hover), not page data or modal state.

Page-level state and handlers should live in a separate hook, similar to usePropertyDetailsState.ts.

Custom hooks may manage state, side effects, and orchestration. Components should only render UI and forward events.

# Naming Conventions

Name hooks with useXState or useXController.

Name templates with Template.

Name presentational components without use or State.

Side Effects

API calls, mutations, and side effects must live in hooks or service files, not directly in components or templates.

# Mock Data

When mocking data, always create a mock API request (function or handler), not static mock objects.

The mock request must:

Accept the inferred or known parameters the real endpoint would require.

Return mock JSON shaped exactly as the UI consumes.

Infer the minimum required parameters from UI usage if docs are unavailable (e.g. propertyId, noteId, fileId) and do not invent extras.

# Design System Read ME 
- Every so often, update the design system read me so it's updated with recent changes